  "result": "Fixed the option ordering and confirmed with the test suite, so I'm wrapping up.\n\nThe cause was in `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py`. It sorted an option's names by prefix length in reverse, so long names came before short ones. Help showed `--help, -h` instead of `-h, --help`. I removed `reverse=True`, so short prefixes come first again. That matches what `tests/test_commands.py` expects.\n\nI looked at `format_options`, `get_params` and the decorator parameter ordering and found nothing wrong there. The full suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). I didn't add a new test for this.\n\nIf the odd order you saw was something else, such as options listed in the wrong sequence rather than names within one option, send me an example of the help output and I'll look again.",
